    bioHtml={[
      'Tuzdy brings a contemplative, reflective voice rooted in Scripture and the tradition of the Catholic Church. As a pediatrician and mother of four, she has spent years watching children grow — in her clinic, on playgrounds, at church, and around her own kitchen table — and has become deeply convinced that every person longs to know who they are and what they were made for.',
      'Before becoming Catholic, Tuzdy chased the cultural version of &ldquo;enough&rdquo;: the best student, doctor, wife, mother, home, and family. Yet beneath all the striving was a question she had not learned to ask: Who was I created for, and for what purpose?',
      'Through the invitation of a friend, the prayers of others, the prompting of the Holy Spirit, and a deep encounter with the Catholic Church, God transformed her heart and brought her home.',
      'With a passion for <b>The Good</b>, Tuzdy speaks to the dignity and worth of every person — especially young people navigating anxiety, confusion, and the pressure to prove themselves. She believes the good life is not something we achieve through striving, but something we receive by knowing God, trusting His promises, and following Him.',
    ]}
    focusHtml="<b>Quote of the Mission:</b><br />&ldquo;You formed my inward parts, you knitted me together in my mother's womb. I praise you, for I am wondrously made.&rdquo; — Psalm 139:13&ndash;14<br /><br /><b>Saint of the Mission:</b><br />St. Mary Magdalene<br />&ldquo;I was one way, and now I am completely different. And the thing that happened in between was Him.&rdquo; — <i>The Chosen</i><br /><br /><b>Favorite pastime:</b><br />Running, pondering, time with friends and family"
